UPDATE companies SET description='Bridon American Corporation operates from Exeter, Pennsylvania, as the U.S. arm of Bekaert''s rope division. Bekaert, a global leader in steel wire transformation and coating technologies, traces its rope-making heritage back more than 300 years, while the modern corporation builds on over 140 years of innovation in materials and manufacturing. The business brings together centuries of rope-making expertise with Bekaert''s strengths in technology and innovation to serve mission-critical applications worldwide.

The company manufactures precision-engineered steel wire ropes and synthetic ropes under the Bridon® and Bexco® brands. Its product portfolio covers mooring, towing, lifting, and hauling ropes for heavy-duty use. Beyond manufacturing, Bridon American provides Ropes360® services, including installation of reels up to 450 metric tons with on-site splicing and socketing, visual and advanced non-destructive inspections, forensic laboratory testing of new and retired ropes, repair and maintenance such as re-lubrication and re-socketing, training, and custom design with tailored logistics and consignment stocking.

Customers span renewable energy, oil and gas, mining, cranes and industrial, and commercial fishing. In renewable energy, the ropes are used on wind turbine installation vessels. Oil and gas clients rely on them for offshore drilling, marine riser tensioners, and offshore lifting. Mining operations use shovel ropes, dragline ropes, and drum winder ropes. Crane applications include offshore cranes, telescopic mobile cranes, and industrial hoist ropes. Commercial fishing fleets employ trawl warps and purse wires.

Bekaert positions its rope business around four legacy strengths: heritage in mission-critical rope manufacturing, technology leadership and innovation, deep understanding of market needs, and global presence with local expertise. The company emphasizes a "better together" approach, co-creating solutions with customers to extend rope life, maximize safety, and reduce downtime through integrated inspection, testing, and maintenance services.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Steel wire rope manufacturing", "Synthetic rope manufacturing", "Rope installation", "Rope inspection (visual, MRT, advanced)", "Non-destructive examination (NDE)", "Post-retirement examination", "Rope testing (forensic lab)", "Rope repair and maintenance (splicing, re-socketing, slip and cut, re-lubrication)", "Rope training", "Technical expert advice", "Custom rope design", "Specialized end terminations", "Custom reels", "Tailored logistics", "Consignment stocking"], "industries": ["Renewable Energy", "Oil & Gas", "Mining", "Cranes & Industrial", "Commercial Fishing"], "materials": ["Steel wire", "Synthetic fibers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Ropes360\u00ae services covering both steel wire and synthetic ropes", "Installation of rope reels up to 450T with on-site splicing, socketing, and welding", "Forensic lab analysis for new, in-service, and retired ropes", "Bekaert Ropes Technology Centre in Doncaster, UK for comprehensive testing", "Custom services: bespoke rope design, specialized end terminations, custom reels, tailored logistics, consignment stocking"], "facts_used": ["HQ Exeter, Pennsylvania -> db", "Part of Bekaert, global leader in steel wire transformation and coating technologies -> /about-us", "Over 140 years of innovation, legacy spanning 300+ years in rope manufacturing -> /, /about-us", "Manufactures precision-engineered steel wire ropes and synthetic ropes (Bridon\u00ae, Bexco\u00ae) -> /, /about-us", "Ropes360\u00ae services: installation, inspection, testing, repair, maintenance, training, custom design -> /services", "Installation capacity up to 450T reels -> /services", "Forensic lab analysis for new, in-service, retired ropes -> /services", "Bekaert Ropes Technology Centre in Doncaster, UK -> /services", "Industries: Renewable Energy (wind turbine installation vessels), Oil & Gas (offshore drilling, MRT, offshore lifting), Mining (shovel, dragline, drum winder ropes), Cranes & Industrial (offshore cranes, telescopic mobile cranes, industrial hoist ropes), Commercial Fishing (trawl warps, purse wires) -> /", "Four legacy strengths: heritage, technology leadership, market understanding, global presence -> /about-us", "Materials: steel wire, synthetic fibers -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Bekaert is a global leader in steel wire transformation and coating technologies.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bridon-american-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Brigade Packaging operates from its headquarters in Jersey City, New Jersey, with an additional office in Dover, Delaware. The company ships products from warehouses on both the West Coast in California and the East Coast in New Jersey to serve customers across the United States. No founding year or ownership details are publicly disclosed.

The company functions as a wholesale packaging supplier, offering a broad catalog of glass, plastic, metal, and paper containers. Its product range includes vials, bottles, jars, tubes, bags, wraps, labels, and closures for pharmaceutical, nutraceutical, cosmetic, and specialty markets.

Brigade Packaging serves industries such as pharmaceuticals, nutraceuticals, beauty and cosmetics, CBD and essential oils, food and beverages, body and skincare, cleaning and industrial, haircare, candles, hand sanitizers, e-liquids, and pet care. Its customer base includes pharmacies, laboratories, product manufacturers, distributors, veterinary clinics, and retailers.

