UPDATE companies SET description='Bright Home Energy operates from Phoenix, Arizona. The company has been installing solar and battery systems for eight years and has powered more than 6,000 homes across the Phoenix metro area, including Mesa.

The company designs, installs, and services residential solar photovoltaic and battery storage systems, working with Tesla Powerwall, SolarEdge, and Enphase equipment. In-house engineering models each system to the individual roof before installation. Beyond solar, Bright Home Energy provides home-performance upgrades including Aeroseal duct sealing — which reduces post-seal leakage to 10% or less — and R-49 blown-in attic insulation with air sealing. The firm handles permitting, utility interconnection, and ongoing production monitoring, backing its work with a 25-year workmanship warranty.

Bright Home Energy serves homeowners in the Phoenix metropolitan area, with a focus on the desert climate that delivers roughly 300 days of sun per year. Typical residential projects range from $18,000 to $34,000 before the 30% federal tax credit. The company also coordinates roof replacement through its sister firm, Bright Home Construction, allowing a single scaffolding setup for both trades.

Bright Home Energy positions itself as an engineering-first installer that is certified on three major storage platforms without sales quotas, enabling unbiased recommendations. Its desert-specific design approach accounts for extreme heat and high solar irradiance, and the company guarantees system performance with real-time monitoring and a promise to return to the roof if production falls short.', certifications=ARRAY['Tesla Powerwall Certified Installer','SolarEdge Certified Installer','Enphase Certified Installer','BBB A+ rating']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Solar panel installation", "Battery storage installation (Tesla Powerwall, SolarEdge, Enphase)", "System performance monitoring", "Permitting and utility interconnection", "Aeroseal duct sealing", "Attic insulation (R-49 blown-in cellulose or fiberglass)", "Home energy audits", "25-year workmanship warranty", "Equipment warranty claims management", "Roof replacement coordination (via sister company)"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Residential battery storage", "Home energy efficiency", "Duct sealing", "Attic insulation"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Lithium-ion batteries", "Cellulose insulation", "Fiberglass insulation", "Aeroseal sealant"], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall", "SolarEdge inverters", "Enphase microinverters", "Aeroseal duct sealing system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Installation 1-3 days; permit-to-operate ~14 days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified installer for Tesla Powerwall, SolarEdge, and Enphase", "In-house system engineering modeled to the shingle", "25-year workmanship warranty with production monitoring", "Aeroseal duct sealing achieving \u226410% post-seal leakage", "R-49 attic insulation with air sealing and 30% federal credit eligibility"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "8 years installing, 6,000+ homes powered -> /", "Certified installer for Tesla Powerwall, SolarEdge, Enphase -> /", "In-house engineering design -> /", "Aeroseal duct sealing with \u226410% leakage -> /", "R-49 attic insulation with air sealing -> /", "25-year workmanship warranty -> /", "Real-time production monitoring -> /", "Desert-specific design for Phoenix climate -> /", "Typical project cost $18,000-$34,000 before tax credit -> /", "Installation 1-3 days, permit-to-operate ~14 days -> /", "Sister company Bright Home Construction for roofing -> /", "BBB A+ rating, 4.9 Google rating -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Engineered, installed and serviced by Bright Home Energy.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bright-home-energy' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bright Services LLC is an electrical contractor headquartered in Bend, Oregon, serving the surrounding Central Oregon region. The company was founded by electricians with 18 years of industry experience who set out to become Bend''s go-to electrical contractor. No founding year is publicly disclosed, and ownership details such as family or veteran status are not specified.

The firm provides a full range of electrical installation and repair services for both commercial and residential construction. Its capabilities include commercial electrical construction, residential wiring for custom and tract homes, multi-family housing projects, electrical panel upgrades, generator installation, low-voltage systems, and general inspections and repairs. The company operates with a team of licensed and bonded electricians, though facility size and headcount are not published.

Bright Services works with residential homeowners, commercial builders, and developers across Central Oregon. Notable project types include medical buildings, apartment complexes, custom single-family homes, and tract housing developments. The company emphasizes tailored estimates rather than fixed pricing, and offers a one-year warranty on materials and labor.

The business was started with a mission to deliver reliable, communicative service in a trade often criticized for inconsistency. Its founders cite three pillars—reliability, respect, and resilience—as the foundation of their approach, promising timely work, careful treatment of client property, and persistent problem-solving on complex jobs.', certifications=ARRAY['Oregon CCB License #237330']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial electrical construction", "Residential electrical construction", "Electrical panel installation and upgrade", "Generator installation", "Electrical inspections and repairs", "Low voltage wiring", "Outlet installation and rewiring", "Custom home wiring", "Tract home wiring", "Multi-family housing electrical work"], "industries": ["Medical buildings", "Multi-family housing", "Custom homes", "Tract homes", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Licensed and bonded electricians on every job", "One-year warranty on materials and labor", "Custom project estimates instead of fixed pricing", "Commitment to consistent communication throughout the project", "Service across Bend and Central Oregon communities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bend, Oregon -> /", "Founded after 18 years of industry experience -> /about", "Mission to be Bend''s go-to electrical contractor -> /about", "Licensed and bonded electricians -> /", "One-year warranty on materials and labor -> /", "Custom estimates based on project needs -> /", "Services: commercial construction, residential construction, electrical panels, generators, inspections & repairs, installation, low voltage -> /", "Industries served: medical buildings, multi-family housing, custom homes, tract homes -> /, /about", "Service area: Bend and Central Oregon -> /", "CCB# 237330 -> /", "Pillars: reliability, respect, resilience -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company