UPDATE companies SET description='Brook Field Service operates from Northfield, Vermont, and has served Northern New York and New England for nearly 40 years as a generator sales and service provider.

The company provides generator installation, maintenance, and repair for all brands, along with standby power system design, transfer switch and battery backup installation, complete system engineering, load bank testing, and preventative maintenance agreements. It also offers generator rentals, financing, onsite evaluations, electrical service upgrades, and FLO EV charger installation. Technicians are factory-trained and TQP-certified for generator and transfer switch repairs, and the firm maintains Northern New England''s largest generator fleet to support 24/7 emergency service. All installations receive engineering supervisory coverage and job-site load testing before handover.

Customers range from residential homeowners to commercial and institutional clients, including hospitals, nursing homes, banks, construction equipment firms, Vermont state agencies requiring emergency generator inspections, and small businesses. Service territory covers Vermont, Maine, New Hampshire, New York, and Massachusetts.

Brook Field Service distinguishes itself as the only Vermont company that troubleshoots and repairs generators, engines, and transfer switches with every employee cross-trained in all three disciplines, so a single service call covers the full system. Its operating philosophy emphasizes integrity, superior service over automation (no robot voices or answering machines), honest communication, and treating employees as revenue sources rather than expenses.', certifications=ARRAY['TQP Certified for Generator and Automatic Transfer Switch Repairs']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Generator installation", "Generator maintenance and repair", "Standby power system design", "Transfer switch installation and repair", "Battery backup system installation", "Complete system design and engineering", "Emergency power solutions", "Load bank testing", "Preventative maintenance agreements", "Electrical service upgrades", "FLO EV charger installation", "Generator rentals", "Financing options", "Onsite evaluation", "Warranty administration", "24/7 emergency service", "Factory-trained technician service", "TQP-certified generator and transfer switch repair", "Sales of Briggs & Stratton, Kohler, and other generator brands", "Generator engine repair", "Automatic transfer switch repair"], "industries": ["Residential", "Healthcare (hospitals and nursing homes)", "Financial services (banks)", "Construction", "Government (Vermont state emergency generator)", "Small business", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only Vermont company that troubleshoots and repairs generators, engines, and transfer switches with all employees cross-trained", "Northern New England''s largest generator fleet", "24/7 emergency service coverage with no automated phone systems", "All installations include engineering supervisory coverage and job-site load testing", "Factory-trained, TQP-certified technicians for generator and transfer switch repairs"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Northfield, Vermont -> db", "Operating for nearly 40 years -> /about", "Provides generator sales, installation, maintenance, and repair -> /, /about", "Services all brands of generators -> /, /about", "Offers 24/7 emergency service -> /, /about", "Claims to be only Vermont company troubleshooting generators, engines, and transfer switches with cross-trained employees -> /about", "Northern New England''s largest generator fleet -> /about", "Technicians are factory-trained and TQP certified -> /", "Serves residential, healthcare, financial, construction, government, and small business customers -> /about", "Service area includes Vermont, Maine, New Hampshire, New York, Massachusetts -> /", "Provides load bank testing and preventative maintenance agreements -> /about", "Offers generator rentals and financing -> /", "Installs FLO EV chargers and electrical service upgrades -> /", "Operating philosophy includes integrity, superior service, honest communication -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Generators for Sale & Rent in Vermont", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='brook-field-service' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Brooklyn WoodWorking operates from Brooklyn, New York, where it has provided custom millwork and solid-surface fabrication for over a decade. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but its website notes more than ten years of experience and over 260 completed projects.

The shop designs, fabricates, and installs custom cabinetry, furniture, and architectural millwork for both residential and commercial clients. Its capabilities span framed and frameless cabinetry, reception desks, teller lines, nurse''s stations, hospital and dental casework, library end panels, and canopy tops. It also produces solid-surface countertops using brands such as Corian®, Avonite®, HI-MACS®, and others, partnering with Corian New York and Solid Surface New York for material supply and installation. The company states it uses state-of-the-art technology and custom-designed equipment in its manufacturing processes.

Residential customers include homeowners, remodelers, and home builders. Commercial work covers professional offices, retail spaces, multi-family dwellings, healthcare facilities, and libraries, often in collaboration with architectural firms. The firm emphasizes scheduling flexibility and on-time delivery as part of its customer-care approach.

