The company serves original equipment manufacturers and other businesses requiring outsourced electronic assembly; specific industry sectors are not enumerated in public materials. A notable reference point is the company''s statement that many current customers have been engaged since the 1990 start date. The firm''s longevity in the market suggests stability for supply chain planning.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Through-hole (THT) PCB assembly", "Surface-mount (SMT) PCB assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Cable assembly", "Complete unit (box-build) assembly", "Conformal coating", "Prototype to production manufacturing"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Many current customers have been with the company since its 1990 start", "Prototype to production capability", "Complete conformal coating available", "THT and SMT circuit board assembly under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1990 -> /", "Located in Brundidge, Alabama -> /", "Provides THT and SMT circuit board assembly -> /", "Provides wire harness and cable assembly -> /", "Provides complete unit assembly -> /", "Offers conformal coating -> /", "Prototype to production capability -> /", "Many customers since 1990 -> /", "Company name Brundidge Electronics Corporation -> db", "Headquarters city Brundidge -> db", "Headquarters state Alabama -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "our wide range of manufacturing services, including THT and SMT circuit board assembly, wire harness and cable assembly, and complete unit assembly", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='brundidge-electronics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company traces its origins to 1922 when William H. Bryce Sr. developed waxing technology at the Dixie Company in Dallas, Texas. He founded Dixie Wax Paper in Memphis in 1927, and in 1969 William H. Bryce Jr. established Bryce Corporation to convert polypropylene films for the snack food market. The business remains family-owned and operated, now in its fourth generation under Chairman and CEO Thomas J. Bryce, who took the helm in 1997, alongside his sons-in-law Sean Bowie and Stephen Perkins.

The company specializes in film conversion and flexible packaging production, offering flexographic printing, lamination, slitting, perforation, pouch making, and logistics. Through affiliate Cyber Graphics it provides design, prepress, and plate-making services, while minority-owned partner Johnson Bryce adds waxing and coating capabilities. Facilities in the Southeast support large-volume runs with automated quality systems including statistical process control, 100% web detection, and a closed-loop quality system. The operation is Safe Quality Food (SQF) certified.

Bryce serves the food, snack, pet care, household, and health and beauty sectors, with specific markets including salty snacks, confectionery, pet food, bakery, frozen foods, and personal care. Its packaging protects products for nationally recognized brands across these categories.

