UPDATE companies SET description='Buck Mason Knitting Mills operates in Mohnton, Pennsylvania, a town with a century-long tradition of shirt manufacturing. After the sudden closure of a factory that had run continuously for 100 years, Buck Mason co-founders Erik and Sasha acquired the facility and rehired its workforce, restarting production within months.

The mill houses knitting machines that enable the company to develop proprietary fabrics from raw yarn, alongside sewing equipment for garment assembly. The operation focuses on t-shirt production, with the capability to control fabric development from scratch.

The company serves the apparel and textile manufacturing sectors, primarily producing for its own Buck Mason brand.

The acquisition was driven by a desire to vertically integrate Buck Mason''s supply chain, revive domestic manufacturing, and preserve the skilled workforce of Mohnton. The founders viewed the existing factory as a sound business opportunity and a chance to rebuild a piece of American industrial heritage.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Knitting", "Sewing", "Proprietary fabric development"], "industries": ["Apparel manufacturing", "Textile manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Singer knitting machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Existing fully operational factory with knitting machines", "Proprietary fabric development from scratch", "Rehired experienced local workforce"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Mohnton, Pennsylvania -> db", "Founders: Erik and Sasha (Buck Mason co-founders) -> /", "Acquired a 100-year-old shirt factory that had closed -> /", "Factory includes knitting machines for proprietary fabric development -> /", "Rehired the factory''s workforce -> /", "Manufactures t-shirts and fabrics -> /", "Uses Singer knitting machines -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /", "Ownership: Private (Buck Mason) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we fired up the Singers and brought the team back to work", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='buck-mason-knitting-mills' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Burnette Foods, Inc. is a third-generation, family-owned food manufacturer headquartered in New Era, Michigan. The company traces its roots to 1935, when Mae and Theodore Sherman purchased a cherry orchard in Central Lake, Michigan, leveraging the region’s sandy soil and Lake Michigan climate. Their son William and his wife Marian later established Sherman Canning Company in East Jordan in 1961, formalizing the family’s entry into food processing. Today, the business operates as Burnette Foods, with production facilities across Michigan.

The company specializes in shelf-stable fruit and vegetable products, including canned dry-pack beans, applesauce, fruit fillings, pumpkin, hummus, fruit cups, meat items, salads, and fruit juices. State-of-the-art processing facilities handle canning, packaging, and private-label production for national and regional brands.

Burnette Foods serves private-label customers, grocery retailers, and food-service distributors seeking a single source for a wide variety of shelf-stable items. Its customer base includes brands that place their own labels on the company’s products, as well as distributors stocking shelves and kitchens nationwide. The company emphasizes long-standing corporate relationships built through experienced sales and customer-service teams.

Burnette Foods differentiates itself through integrity, innovation, and forward-thinking practices. Its processing aims to retain the flavor, color, texture, and nutrient integrity of fruits and vegetables. Sustainability initiatives include water and energy reduction, recycling of corrugated and tin packaging, upcycling fruit pits, and converting by-products into livestock feed.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shelf-stable food processing", "Canning", "Private label packaging", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Meat and salad production", "Sustainable processing (water/energy reduction, recycling, upcycling)", "Sales and customer service"], "industries": ["Shelf-stable fruit and vegetable manufacturing", "Private label food manufacturing", "Food distribution", "Grocery retail", "Food service"], "materials": ["Fruits", "Vegetables", "Beans", "Meat"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1935 when Mae and Theodore Sherman purchased a cherry orchard in Central Lake, Michigan -> /about", "Sherman Canning Company established in 1961 by William and Marian Sherman -> /about", "Third-generation family-owned business -> /about", "Headquartered in New Era, Michigan -> db", "Produces shelf-stable fruits and vegetables including canned beans, applesauce, fruit fillings, pumpkin, hummus, fruit cups, meat items, salads, fruit juices -> /", "Operates production facilities throughout Michigan -> /about", "One of the nation''s largest producers of shelf-stable fruits and vegetables -> /about", "Sustainability practices: water/energy reduction, recycling packaging, upcycling fruit pits, livestock feed from by-product -> /", "Certifications: Organic, Non-GMO, Kosher, USDA, FDA, Gluten-free on several products -> products list", "Private label services for customer brands -> /", "Responsive, committed, personalized service with experienced sales and customer service teams -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Makers of shelf-stable products for three generations.", "founded_year": "1935", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='burnette-foods-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Burns Electric, headquartered in Des Moines, Iowa, has operated as an electrical utility contractor across the Midwest for more than 40 years. The company provides integrated construction, maintenance, and emergency services for power delivery infrastructure.

Its service portfolio spans overhead and underground distribution, transmission installation and maintenance from 69 kV to 345 kV, substation civil and electrical work, street and facility lighting, and 24/7 storm restoration. Crews handle most scopes in‑house and partner with specialists for turnkey projects.

