UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Precision Switchgear operates from Concord, North Carolina, in the Charlotte metropolitan area. The company was founded in 2006 by Doug Weaver, a former U.S. Navy interior communications specialist who spent 24 years as a nuclear supervisor at Duke Energy performing power-factor testing and circuit-breaker repair. Weaver launched the business to provide specialized refurbishing and testing services for low- and medium-voltage switchgear.

The firm’s core work is restoring circuit breakers to original performance through a full disassembly, cleaning, plating (silver or dichromate), repair, and reassembly process carried out by Level II PEARL‑certified technicians. A 10,000‑square‑foot facility houses calibrated test equipment including primary‑injection sets, while mobile trailers bring the same capabilities to customer sites. Through its affiliation with Group CBS, the company also offers engineering support, training, and access to over 800 CBS ArcSafe remote‑racking and remote‑switching products.

Customers span utilities, manufacturing plants, and commercial facilities. The shop services equipment from major manufacturers such as ABB, GE, Westinghouse/Eaton, Siemens, Square D, and Federal Pacific, as well as obsolete brands. Services range from preventive maintenance and infrared thermography to arc‑flash studies, high‑current testing, cable VLF/tan‑delta testing, and emergency troubleshooting.

The company emphasizes that reconditioning existing breakers can cost roughly 30 % of a new retrofill installation, saving customers tens of thousands of dollars. Its differentiation rests on the combination of in‑shop and on‑site capabilities, PEARL‑certified personnel, and the parts inventory and remote‑operation tools supplied by the Group CBS network.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Circuit breaker refurbishing", "Switchgear repair", "Primary injection testing", "Secondary injection testing", "DC primary injection testing", "Medium voltage relay testing", "Transformer testing", "Infrared thermography", "Arc flash studies", "Power quality testing", "Cable testing (VLF/Tan Delta)", "AC high current testing", "DC high current testing", "Remote racking solutions", "Remote switch operators", "Remote switch actuators & kits", "Silver plating", "Dichromate plating", "Engineering services", "Training services", "Outage planning", "Troubleshooting & emergency calls", "Preventive maintenance", "Electrical inspections"], "industries": ["Utilities", "Manufacturing", "Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Silver", "Dichromate"], "equipment": ["Primary injection test set", "CBS ArcSafe Remote Racking Solutions", "CBS ArcSafe Remote Switch Operators", "CBS ArcSafe Remote Switch Actuators & Kits"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Level II PEARL\u2011certified technicians perform all refurbishing and testing", "10,000 sq. ft. facility with calibrated primary\u2011injection test sets", "Mobile trailers equipped for on\u2011site primary/secondary injection and infrared inspection", "Access to 800+ CBS ArcSafe remote\u2011racking and remote\u2011switching products", "Refurbishing typically costs 30\u202f% of a new retrofill installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Concord, NC -> db", "10,000 sq ft facility -> /, /services", "Level II PEARL certified technicians -> /, /about-us", "Mobi